{"note":"Where each species is known from dated sites. Areas on the map are soft outlines around the sites active at a time, not population maps. Site ages are approximate ranges in ka. Homo sapiens: each land cell is filled from the time people could first have reached it, spreading ~1,000 km per thousand years from the African sites and from the migration routes as they advance (data/routes.json), while it is dry land and not under ice.","species":[{"id":"neanderthal","color":"#f2a65a","ko":["네안데르탈인","유럽과 서아시아, 멀리 알타이까지 살았던 인류. 약 4만 년 전 무렵 사라졌지만 그 DNA는 오늘날 사람들 안에 남아 있습니다."],"en":["Neanderthals","People of Europe and western Asia, reaching as far as the Altai. They disappeared around 40,000 years ago, but their DNA lives on in people today."],"sites":[{"n":"Ehringsdorf","lon":11.32,"lat":50.95,"max":230,"min":190},{"n":"Biache-Saint-Vaast","lon":2.95,"lat":50.31,"max":190,"min":160},{"n":"Saccopastore","lon":12.5,"lat":41.93,"max":250,"min":120},{"n":"Altamura","lon":16.55,"lat":40.8,"max":172,"min":130},{"n":"Krapina","lon":15.87,"lat":46.16,"max":140,"min":120},{"n":"Tabun","lon":34.97,"lat":32.67,"max":140,"min":100},{"n":"Denisova Cave (Neanderthal layers)","lon":84.68,"lat":51.4,"max":140,"min":90},{"n":"Teshik-Tash","lon":67.0,"lat":38.1,"max":75,"min":60},{"n":"Shanidar","lon":44.22,"lat":36.83,"max":75,"min":45},{"n":"Kebara","lon":34.95,"lat":32.56,"max":65,"min":48},{"n":"Amud","lon":35.5,"lat":32.87,"max":60,"min":50},{"n":"Chagyrskaya","lon":83.15,"lat":51.44,"max":60,"min":50},{"n":"Mezmaiskaya","lon":40.0,"lat":44.17,"max":70,"min":40},{"n":"La Ferrassie","lon":0.94,"lat":44.95,"max":55,"min":42},{"n":"La Chapelle-aux-Saints","lon":1.72,"lat":45.0,"max":56,"min":47},{"n":"El Sidrón","lon":-5.33,"lat":43.38,"max":51,"min":46},{"n":"Okladnikov Cave","lon":84.6,"lat":51.6,"max":50,"min":40},{"n":"Feldhofer (Neander Valley)","lon":6.95,"lat":51.23,"max":45,"min":39},{"n":"Vindija","lon":16.08,"lat":46.3,"max":46,"min":40},{"n":"Spy","lon":4.67,"lat":50.48,"max":44,"min":40},{"n":"Gorham's Cave","lon":-5.34,"lat":36.12,"max":45,"min":40},{"n":"Les Cottés","lon":0.6,"lat":46.7,"max":45,"min":40}],"src":[{"label":"Hublin 2009, PNAS","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0904119106"},{"label":"Higham et al. 2014, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13621"}]},{"id":"denisovan","color":"#c79bff","ko":["데니소바인","DNA로 먼저 알려진 인류. 시베리아 알타이에서 티베트고원, 동아시아 북쪽까지 흔적이 있고, 오늘날 오세아니아·동아시아 사람들에게 DNA를 남겼습니다."],"en":["Denisovans","A people first known from DNA. Traces run from the Siberian Altai to the Tibetan Plateau and northern East Asia, and their DNA survives in people of Oceania and East Asia today."],"sites":[{"n":"Denisova Cave","lon":84.68,"lat":51.4,"max":200,"min":50},{"n":"Baishiya Karst Cave","lon":102.57,"lat":35.45,"max":190,"min":45},{"n":"Harbin","lon":126.6,"lat":45.8,"max":170,"min":138},{"n":"Tam Ngu Hao 2 (Cobra Cave)","lon":103.0,"lat":20.2,"max":164,"min":131}],"dispute":{"ko":"라오스 탐 응우 하오 2의 어금니가 데니소바인의 것인지는 확실하지 않습니다. 하얼빈 머리뼈의 이름(호모 롱기)도 논쟁 중입니다.","en":"Whether the Tam Ngu Hao 2 molar in Laos is Denisovan is uncertain, and the name of the Harbin skull (Homo longi) is debated."},"src":[{"label":"Slon et al. 2018, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-018-0455-x"},{"label":"Chen et al. 2019, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1139-x"},{"label":"Demeter et al. 2022, Nat. Commun.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29923-z"},{"label":"Ji et al. 2021, The Innovation","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xinn.2021.100132"}]},{"id":"erectus","color":"#e3d27a","ko":["호모 에렉투스 (마지막 무리)","백만 년 넘게 아시아에 살았던 인류의 마지막 흔적은 자와섬에 있습니다."],"en":["Homo erectus (last populations)","The last traces of a human that lived in Asia for over a million years are on Java."],"sites":[{"n":"Ngandong","lon":111.33,"lat":-7.37,"max":117,"min":108}],"src":[{"label":"Rizal et al. 2019, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1863-2"}]},{"id":"floresiensis","color":"#8fe3b0","ko":["플로레스인","인도네시아 플로레스섬에만 살았던 작은 인류입니다."],"en":["Homo floresiensis","A small human known only from the island of Flores, Indonesia."],"sites":[{"n":"Liang Bua","lon":120.46,"lat":-8.53,"max":190,"min":50}],"src":[{"label":"Sutikna et al. 2016, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature17179"}]},{"id":"luzonensis","color":"#7fd6e0","ko":["루손인","필리핀 루손섬의 작은 인류입니다."],"en":["Homo luzonensis","A small human from Luzon in the Philippines."],"sites":[{"n":"Callao Cave","lon":121.82,"lat":17.7,"max":67,"min":50}],"src":[{"label":"Détroit et al. 2019, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1067-9"}]},{"id":"naledi","color":"#f08fb0","ko":["호모 날레디","남아프리카의 작은 뇌를 가진 인류로, 현생인류가 나타나던 무렵에도 살아 있었습니다."],"en":["Homo naledi","A small-brained human of southern Africa, alive when our own species was appearing."],"sites":[{"n":"Rising Star Cave","lon":27.73,"lat":-26.02,"max":335,"min":236}],"src":[{"label":"Dirks et al. 2017, eLife","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.24231"}]},{"id":"sapiens","color":"#4aa3ff","followsRoutes":true,"ko":["현생인류 (호모 사피엔스)","아프리카 여러 곳에서 모습을 갖춘 뒤, 약 6만~4만 5천 년 전부터 세계 곳곳으로 퍼졌습니다. 아프리카 밖의 영역은 이동 경로를 따라 넓어집니다."],"en":["Homo sapiens","Took shape across many parts of Africa, then spread around the world from about 60,000–45,000 years ago. Outside Africa the area grows along the migration routes."],"sites":[{"n":"Jebel Irhoud","lon":-8.87,"lat":31.85,"max":315,"min":0},{"n":"Omo Kibish","lon":35.92,"lat":5.4,"max":233,"min":0},{"n":"Herto","lon":40.5,"lat":10.3,"max":160,"min":0},{"n":"Pinnacle Point","lon":22.1,"lat":-34.2,"max":164,"min":0},{"n":"Blombos Cave","lon":21.22,"lat":-34.41,"max":100,"min":0}],"src":[{"label":"Hublin et al. 2017, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22336"},{"label":"Vidal et al. 2022, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-04275-8"},{"label":"White et al. 2003, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature01669"},{"label":"Marean et al. 2007, Nature","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06204"},{"label":"Groucutt et al. 2015, E